      "message": "Yes! aosp/2976058 adds 3 measurements. 1) getting the new transactions and writing them to the file, 2) the existing call to `dump_backtrace_to_file_timeout` and 3) for the `fdatasync` call.\n\nI built and booted `aosp_cf_x86_64_phone-trunk_staging-userdebug` on my Cloudtop.\n```\nadb root\nadb shell am hang\n# in another shell\nadb logcat | grep Microseconds\n```\nAfter the ANR happens I grabbed the logs and checked them.\nRaw logs: https://paste.googleplex.com/6660839681032192\n\n```\n~/workspace/aosp/main/frameworks/av$ cat raw_data.txt | grep transactions | awk \u0027END {print s} NF\u003e1{s +\u003d $NF}\u0027 \n47296\n~/workspace/aosp/main/frameworks/av$ cat raw_data.txt | grep backtrace | awk \u0027END {print s} NF\u003e1{s +\u003d $NF}\u0027 \n1425946\n~/workspace/aosp/main/frameworks/av$ cat raw_data.txt | grep fdatasync | awk \u0027END {print s} NF\u003e1{s +\u003d $NF}\u0027 \n153988\n```\n\nIt looks like the total time spent doing these three operations during an ANR on CF is 1) 47ms, 2) 1400ms, 3) 150ms. 47/(1400+150) \u003d ~3% additional time.\n\nDoes that sound/look right? Is there anything else I can do differently?\n\nI\u0027ll add the final data to the bug once we have enough info.",
